{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/948434-five-dragon-style","id":948434,"title":"Five-Dragon Style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-11T01:04:02-07:00","id":948434,"title":"Five-Dragon Style","content":"I've been looking around for a while for some homebrews of the Immaculate MA styles since 3E came out and so far I've come up short. In an effort to bring one of my characters into 3E I've worked on the beginnings of Five-Dragon Style and wanted to run them by the community here to see what you guys think.<br /> <br /> <b><u>Five-Dragon Style</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Form Weapons:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> Unarmed Strikes, Straight Swords and Lances</span></span><br /> <b>Armor:</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"> Five-Dragon Style is compatible with up to Medium Armor</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Five-Dragon Claw</b>[spoiler]<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering, Terrestrial, Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b>None<br /> Giving her fingers the aspect of the Five Elemental Dragons\u2019claws, whose perfected natures slice through the thickest of godhides, the Martial Artist\u2019s attacks cuts flesh to ribbons without concern for the armor before it. <b>Withering</b> attacks supplemented by this charm Act as if they had the Piercing tag without imposing the penalties of using a Piercing attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Terrestrial:</b> A Dragonblooded who uses this charm suffers the normal penalties for using a Piercing attack.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastery:</b> The strongest of the Exalted may deliver blows that are stopped by nothing. Solar Exalted add their Essence rating to the soak reduction of Piercing attacks supplemented with this charm.[/collapse]<br /> <br /> <b>Five-Dragon-Force Blow</b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual, Terrestrial, Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Five-Dragon Claw<br /> With a brief invocation to the might of the Five Dragons, the Dragon-Blooded martial artist lays out his foe with a single attack.<br /> <br /> This attack doubles the Exalts Strength for the purpose of determining the raw damage of a <b>withering</b> attack, and applies the Smashing tag to the attack without sacrificing a point of Defense to use it. A <b>decisive</b> attack carries over a number of 10s on the attack roll to the damage roll equal to the Exalts Essence score.<br /> <br /> <b>Terrestrial:</b> Dragon-Blooded who use this charm must still sacrifice a point of defense to make use of the Smashing tag with this Charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastery:</b> The Exalt knocks their opponent back with sufficient force to inflict damage equivalent to falling a short distance on a <b>decisive</b> attack.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Five-Dragon Fortitude</b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m per point of initiative; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Terrestrial, Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The resilience of the Dragons is boundless, and beyond petty scrapes and bruises; as are those who seek to emulate their glory. Invoking this Charm in response to a specific attack, the Five-Dragon Stylist gains one initiative for each mote spent. They may not spend more motes on this charm then their (Essence or 3, whichever is higher)+Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3+, Martial Arts 5+ This charm may be repurchased. Doing so removes the Withering-only tag and adds the Dual tag, allowing the Martial Artist to spend 3m to remove a sustained level of damage after a successful <b>decisive</b> attack - subject to the same spending limitations imposed by this charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Terrestrial:</b> A Terrestrial Exalt may only spend up to (Essence or 3, whichever is higher) motes on this charm. - I may need to bump the spending limit on this one up. Thoughts?</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Five-Dragon Blocking Technique</b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1m per point of Parry; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b>One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Five-Dragon Fortitude<br /> <br /> Letting the Dragons guide him, the Exalt aids his defense with Essence. By spending a mote of essence the Martial Artis may increase their Parry by one until the beginning of their next turn, but they may only do so a number of times equal half their essence rounded up. If unarmed they may also parry lethal attacks without a stunt or other magic.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastery:</b>For an additional 2m, 1w a Solar or Abyssal Exalted who knows Five-Dragon Form may Activate this charm while they enter Five-Dragon Form and extend the duration of this charm for as long as they have Five-Dragon Form active.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Five-Dragon Form</b><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 7m <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b>One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Five-Dragon Blocking Technique, Five-Dragon-Force Blow<br /> Performing a quick series of motions that offer thanks and claim guidance from the earth, sky and sea, with the martial artist herself representing fire and life, the Dragon-Blood takes aspects of all five elements into her technique.<br /> <br /> The Five-Dragon stylist's unarmed Martial Arts attacks inflict lethal damage without need for a stunt, and she adds (Higher of Essence or 3) to her soak. If she\u2019s wielding one of the form\u2019s weapons, she treats it as though it has +1 Accuracy. Also, she adds her (Essence or 3, whichever is higher) to her Dexterity or Strength for rolls to perform a Movement Action (Rush, Disengage, Rise from Prone, Take Cover, Withdraw) and for Feats of Strength.<br /> <br /> <b>Special Activation Rules:</b>???<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:tahoma\">I'm having a hard time with the Form Charms special activation trigger, every Form charm has one and this one is eluding me. I'd love some suggestions there.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3558-dunecat","user":"dunecat","date":". 08-19-2016, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3558-dunecat","name":"dunecat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T06:16:49-07:00","id":949270,"title":"","content":"A scene-long +1 to +3 Parry for 3-5m, 1wp is a little too reminiscent of 2e's Infinite Ability Mastery for my comfort. But I'll admit, that might be just me, and moreover, I have no idea what I'd replace it with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T08:57:13-07:00","id":949339,"title":"","content":"They're Style Weapons in 3e. Could you include a description of what it looks like to fight with Five-Dragon Style under Style Weapons? It's one of the really good elements of 3e that helps sell the feel of each MA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:59:59-07:00","id":949418,"title":"","content":"I'd be a little wary of porting the effects over from 2e wholesale. Your opening two Charms are, I think, far and away too good.<br /> <br /> As a thought experiment, consider a Solar with a lance, Strength 3, Martial Arts 5, Five-Dragon Claw, and Five-Dragon-Force Blow. For 3 motes, they're punching through 8 soak and doubling their base withering damage of (Str 3+lance 11) to a damage pool of 28, before extra successes on the attack roll. For reference, one of the hardest nuts to crack in the antagonists chapter is Fakharu, who has a whopping 24 soak and Legendary Size. Without any other considerations, this Solar lops his soak down to 16 and has 12 damage dice - more than enough to ignore Legendary Size's prohibition on crashing. This is all before extra successes, or any other Charms, and all comes at less than your mote regeneration rate. Your decisive damage adders aren't nearly as extreme, but then again they don't really need to be when you've stockpiled incredible amounts of Initiative because you can crash all but the most heavily-defended opponents in one go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11517-bozwevial","name":"Bozwevial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T12:00:48-07:00","id":949459,"title":"","content":"Back when I was tinkering with the system during the playtest, I did a version of FDS and spruced it up/ruined it. The original purpose was to get a feel for tinkering with the system and the balance. I think it's OK at best. Crescens even helped me make a PDF, wonderful man that he is.<br /> <br /> You can help yourself to anything you want in this for you own use, OP. I love 5DS because sometimes you just want simple and effective. It'd be a great loss to see it not make it into EX3, and I don't expect we will see it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Don't worry about the stuff at the end of the PDF. That's just an untenable road.<br /> <br /> Double Edit: This was also done before they changed the Celestial keyword to Terrestrial.<br /> <br /> Link: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/u2k8mrj9dmw0v6e/Five%20Dragon%20Style%20v4.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/u2k8mrj9dm...%20v4.pdf?dl=0</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":255,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","user":"ParanoiaCombo","date":". 08-12-2016, 03:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T22:01:59-07:00","id":949834,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback everyone. I appreciate it! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/948434-five-dragon-style?p=949270#post949270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A scene-long +1 to +3 Parry for 3-5m, 1wp is a little too reminiscent of 2e's Infinite Ability Mastery for my comfort. But I'll admit, that might be just me, and moreover, I have no idea what I'd replace it with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Holding to the intent of the initial charm does impose that problem. I could cut the durations down and cut the 1w from the cost, making the base version last one tick and the Mastery version untill the start of your next turn.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/948434-five-dragon-style?p=949339#post949339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're Style Weapons in 3e. Could you include a description of what it looks like to fight with Five-Dragon Style under Style Weapons? It's one of the really good elements of 3e that helps sell the feel of each MA.</div> </div> </div> </div> Good point! I'll work on it, though I'm working tomorrow so I doubt I'll have anything up until Sunday.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bozwevial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/948434-five-dragon-style?p=949418#post949418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be a little wary of porting the effects over from 2e wholesale. Your opening two Charms are, I think, far and away too good.<br /> <br /> As a thought experiment, consider a Solar with a lance, Strength 3, Martial Arts 5, Five-Dragon Claw, and Five-Dragon-Force Blow. For 3 motes, they're punching through 8 soak and doubling their base withering damage of (Str 3+lance 11) to a damage pool of 28, before extra successes on the attack roll. For reference, one of the hardest nuts to crack in the antagonists chapter is Fakharu, who has a whopping 24 soak and Legendary Size. Without any other considerations, this Solar lops his soak down to 16 and has 12 damage dice - more than enough to ignore Legendary Size's prohibition on crashing. This is all before extra successes, or any other Charms, and all comes at less than your mote regeneration rate. Your decisive damage adders aren't nearly as extreme, but then again they don't really need to be when you've stockpiled incredible amounts of Initiative because you can crash all but the most heavily-defended opponents in one go.</div> </div> </div> </div>While you make a good point about the effect of combining those charms, but allow me to suggest a counter comparison; A solar with the same stats, Armor Penetrating Fang Strike (Snake Style) and Thunderbold Attack Prana. On a withering attack they ignore all of a targets armor based soak and double successes on the damage roll - including damage rolled from extra sucesses on the attack roll. <br /> <br /> Admittedly a Lance is more powerful then Sank's style weapons but access to Striking Cobra Technique adds Dex to the raw damage, which will probably be +5. Also worth consideration is that APFS only negates armor soak, so Fakharu wouldn't be bothered by it where as Five-Dragon Claw is universally applicable, which I felt offset the difference in how much soak is reduced. I did however fail to note the conditional activation part of APFS where you have to have higher Initiative. <br /> <br /> I suppose I could apply the same design approach that I used with the Smashing tag in Five-Dragon-Force Blow and simply allow it to add the Piercing tag to an attack, with the Mastery version permitting that it be used without the defense penalty, or somethign similar. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/948434-five-dragon-style?p=949459#post949459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back when I was tinkering with the system during the playtest, I did a version of FDS and spruced it up/ruined it. The original purpose was to get a feel for tinkering with the system and the balance. I think it's OK at best. Crescens even helped me make a PDF, wonderful man that he is.<br /> <br /> You can help yourself to anything you want in this for you own use, OP. I love 5DS because sometimes you just want simple and effective. It'd be a great loss to see it not make it into EX3, and I don't expect we will see it.<br /> <br /> Edit: Don't worry about the stuff at the end of the PDF. That's just an untenable road.<br /> <br /> Double Edit: This was also done before they changed the Celestial keyword to Terrestrial.<br /> <br /> Link: <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/u2k8mrj9dmw0v6e/Five%20Dragon%20Style%20v4.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/u2k8mrj9dm...%20v4.pdf?dl=0</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I'm sure this will be a big help! I hope that FDS makes it through into 3E, for a lot of the same reasons you like it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3558-dunecat","name":"dunecat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T06:24:38-07:00","id":950000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dunecat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/948434-five-dragon-style?p=949834#post949834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While you make a good point about the effect of combining those charms, but allow me to suggest a counter comparison; A solar with the same stats, Armor Penetrating Fang Strike (Snake Style) and Thunderbold Attack Prana. On a withering attack they ignore all of a targets armor based soak and double successes on the damage roll - including damage rolled from extra sucesses on the attack roll.<br /> <br /> Admittedly a Lance is more powerful then Sank's style weapons but access to Striking Cobra Technique adds Dex to the raw damage, which will probably be +5. Also worth consideration is that APFS only negates armor soak, so Fakharu wouldn't be bothered by it where as Five-Dragon Claw is universally applicable, which I felt offset the difference in how much soak is reduced. I did however fail to note the conditional activation part of APFS where you have to have higher Initiative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure the comparison is really applicable - in the first place, Thunderbolt Attack Prana is Decisive-Only and won't do anything for a withering attack! But leaving that out of consideration, having both those two together requires you to have bought seven charms (to our Five-Dragon Solar's two), and they cost 4m 1wp and 5m 1wp respectively (to the combined 3m of the two Five-Dragon charms). They're considerably more of an investment, and the Willpower cost prevents their frequent use.<br /> <br /> Putting more of a direct comparison on paper, Armor-Piercing Fang Strike ignores all your enemy's armored soak - 3 to 7 points for mundane armor, 5 to 11 points for artifact armor, and probably outlier values for rarer opponents. Compare Five-Dragon Claw, which for a much cheaper cost ignores 8 soak flat for a MA 5 Solar. This actually means you come out ahead in soak reduction on anything up to and including light artifact armor, even on medium artifact armor, and three points behind on heavy artifact armor (but you've also saved 4m, 1wp over the cost of Armor-Piercing Fang Strike). So Five-Dragon Claw loses a few points of soak reduction there, but provides a much better soak reduction on basically any other target and does it with a much lower price tag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11517-bozwevial","user":"Bozwevial","date":".  fixed some wording 08-19-2016, 10:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11517-bozwevial","name":"Bozwevial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T07:24:13-07:00","id":953822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bozwevial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/948434-five-dragon-style?p=950000#post950000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure the comparison is really applicable - in the first place, Thunderbolt Attack Prana is Decisive-Only and won't do anything for a withering attack! But leaving that out of consideration, having both those two together require you to have bought seven charms (to our Five-Dragon Solar's two) and cost 4m 1wp and 5m 1wp respectively (to the combined 3m of the two Five-Dragon charms). They're considerably more of an investment, and the Willpower cost prevents their frequent use.<br /> <br /> Putting more of a direct comparison on paper, Armor-Piercing Fang Strike ignores all your enemy's armored soak - 3 to 7 points for mundane armor, 5 to 11 points for artifact armor, and probably outlier values for rarer opponents. Compare Five-Dragon Claw, which for a much cheaper cost ignores 8 soak flat for a MA 5 Solar. This actually means you come out ahead in soak reduction on anything up to and including light artifact armor, even on medium artifact armor, and three points behind on heavy artifact armor (but you've also saved 4m, 1wp over the cost of Armor-Piercing Fang Strike). So Five-Dragon Claw loses a few points of soak reduction there, but provides a much better soak reduction on basically any other target and does it with a much lower price tag.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You make a good point, so I've gone back and tweaked both FD Claw and FD Force Blow. I also worked on some formatting. Should be easier to read now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3558-dunecat","name":"dunecat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T01:13:24-07:00","id":958101,"title":"","content":"So, I've overhauled these considerably after going through the responses here. Thanks for the input guys, and thanks ParanoiaCombo for the use of your PDF. It helped with a few distinct elements and I like the fluff behind the creation of the style you created.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Five-Dragon Style</u></b><br /> <br /> <b>Form Weapons:</b> Unarmed Strikes, Straight Swords, Spears, and Lances<br /> <b>Armor:</b> Five-Dragon Style is compatible with up to Medium Armor<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Five-Dragon Claw<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual, Mastery<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b>None<br /> The Fivefold Dragon bends her will to emulating the rending fury of the Elemental Dragons, whose claws pierce even the thickest of god-hides. Blows made with this charm are enhanced with red and white claws of essence at the users fingertips or that carve the air along the path of their weapons.<b>Withering</b> attacks supplemented with this charm ignore the Fivefold Dragons (Willpower/2 rounded up) soak, with an additional point of soak bypassed if the attack is made barehanded.<br /> <br /> <b>Terrestrial:</b>Dragonblooded must pay an additional 1i to activate this charm.<br /> <br /> <b>Mastery:</b>The strongest of the Exalted may deliver blows that are stopped by nothing. Solar Exalted add their Essence rating to the soak reduction of attacks supplemented with this charm.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It was pointed out that this charm as it stood previously was considerably more powerful then it should be compared to similarly functioning charms. I think with the mechanic calculated off of willpower it represents a greater cost to maximize the soak reduction here as well as reducing the maximum soak reduction. In the case of a barehanded attack it's still as high as -7 soak, but when used armed it caps out at -6, a couple points lower then the initial build was set.</div></div> </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Five-Dragon-Force Blow<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m(+2m); <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual, Terrestrial<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Five-Dragon Claw<br /> The might of the Elemental Dragons cannot be gainsaid and those who follow the path of Five-Dragon Style strive to reach that pinnacle of explosive force. Contracting in on themselves and then expanding through their body in a devastating blow augmented by out-rushing bands red and blue essence.<br /> <br /> This attack doubles the Exalts Strength for the purpose of determining the raw damage of a <b>withering</b> attack while a <b>decisive</b> attack carries over a number of 10s on the attack roll to the damage roll equal to the half (round up) the Exalts Willpower score. Use of this charm with a <b>decisive</b> attack costs an extra 2 motes.<br /> <br /> In either case, compare the results on the damage roll to the targets Stamina+Resistance/2. If more successes are gained then the target is knocked back one range band, or knocked prone. If an additional 3 successes are gained beyond that number then the target is both knocked back and prone.<br /> <br /> When a target is both knocked back and knocked prone the Fivefold Dragon may reflexively enter Five-Dragon Form<br /> <br /> Terrestrial: Replicating the focused power of the Dragons is no easy feat, and the Terrestrial Exalted lack the force of essence to do so without strain. They count their defense as 1 point lower during any turn they use this charm.<br /> <br /> Mastery: The Exalt knocks their opponent back with sufficient force that if they strike an object in mid flight that they take damage as if they fell from a short distance.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">It's the poor man's version of Heaven Thunder Hammer in many ways, though it's also a functional damage adder, which is why I included a difficulty that had to be overcome to accomplish knockdown/back. The conversion of attack roll 10s to damage dice is.. well I'm not quite sure what to make of it. It could mean as much as 5 extra dice on the Initiative roll but it's entirely down to luck, it might not mean any extra dice on that damage roll either.</div></div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Five-Dragon Fortitude<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m per 2 points of initiative; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Withering-only, Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> The resilience of the Dragons is boundless, and beyond petty scrapes and bruises; as are those who seek to emulate their glory. When this charm is activated the Fivefold Dragon is sheathed in translucent white and green scales of essence in response to taking a glancing blow. When they lose initiative to a withering attack this charm allows the Five-Dragon Stylist to gain one initiative for each mote spent; but may not spend more motes then the lowest of their Natural Soak+Willpower or the amount of initiative they lost.<br /> <br /> At Essence 3+, Martial Arts 5+ This charm may be repurchased. Doing so removes the Withering-only tag and adds the Dual tag. By spending 1i the Fivefold Dragon may then spend 3m to negate a sustained level of damage from a successful <b>decisive</b> attack - subject to the same spending limitations imposed by this charm.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">In 2E this was a <i>very</i> efficient soak adder, but with the changes in 3E soak is a much more scarce resource. I wanted to retain the ability to shrug off a fairly substantial blow without trouble as long as the motes were available to spend but didn't want to ignore the built in scarcity of soak. I think this idea of gaining initiative in equal measure to how much you just lost works well; it lets you weather a powerful blow without harm while still allowing your enemy to have gained something from it. Thinking about it some more it'll also probably bump up the potential for decisive damage clashes..</div></div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Five-Dragon Blocking Technique<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 4m,1w; <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Uniform<br /> <b>Duration:</b>Until the start of your next turn<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Five-Dragon Fortitude<br /> <br /> The Elemental Dragons are fierce warriors whose perfected technique rendered them untouchable. The Fivefold Dragon has achieved such mastery of form, blending parry and evasion though it requires immense focus. On activating this charm streaks of blue and black essence trail their motions. They increase their Parry Defense by an amount equal to half their Evasion defense (rounded up, max of 1/2 Willpower (rounded down)).<br /> <br /> If no attacks are able to penetrate the Fivefold Dragons enhanced defenses by the start of their next action, their will is bolstered. restoring 1 point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">IC I picture this as the sort of 'move behind your blade' type of defense rather then the 'swat your opponents weapon away' kind of defense. A literal blend of blocking and the kind of 'dodge by an inch' evasion. Mechanically at it's most efficient you can gain +5 parry for 4m, but that requires both purchasing 10 Willpower, maxing out your Dodge score, and then pushing your Evasion up to 10 with other charms.. which would cost more then just pushing your Parry up with a MA excellency. Keeping that in mind, practical yield on a character with max dex+dodge+specialty (assuming use of Reed in the Wind, and 8+ Willpower ) should be +4 for 3m (assuming the form charm as well) with the chance to lose 1 wp if you don't manage to parry somehow. More efficient then the same buff with just your MA excellency but not breaking your dice cap.. a DB of course would run into their die cap at +3 from this charm. </div></div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Five-Dragon Form<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m <b>Mins:</b> Martial Arts 4, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b>One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Five-Dragon Blocking Technique, Five-Dragon-Force Blow<br /> <br /> Having mastered themselves through shear force of willpower and exceptional technique the Fivefold Dragon has internalized the core of being a dragon; unmatched power, resilience and grace forged together under a relentless will. Embodying this and lending essence to its realization ignites this charm - literally igniting a blaze of essence on the users brow that flickers with the colours and power of all five elements. As a result this charm cannot be used while wearing a helm due to it interfering with the proper flow of essence needed. (I personally encourage the use of dramatic helmet removal as part of the stunt/description of activating this form)<br /> <br /> While in this form the Fivefold Dragon gains the following benefits.<ul><li>Martial Arts attacks inflict lethal damage without need for a stunt.</li> <li>Natural Soak increases by the higher of their Essence or 2</li> <li>If unarmored they gain hardness equal to half their Willpower.</li> <li>While wielding one of the form\u2019s weapons, it is treated as though it has +1 Accuracy.</li> <li>The higher of Essence or 2 is added to their Dexterity or Strength for rolls/pools to perform a Movement Action (Rush, Disengage, Rise from Prone, Take Cover, Withdraw), for Feats of Strength and to actions that involve breaking objects.</li> <li>Finally they reduce the cost of all preceding charms in this style by 1m.</li> </ul><b>Special Activation Rule:</b>Whenever the Fivefold Dragon's Will is bolstered in the form of regaining a point of temporary Willpower, this form may be activated Reflexively.<br /> <br /> <b>Terrestrial:</b> Terrestrial Exalted to not enjoy the full mote discount offered by this charm, and must chose a single preceding charm to gain the reduced activation cost each time this charm is used.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Does a lot of the same things that the 2E charm did, but I grabbed a couple effects from ParanoiaCombo's pdf that I liked (particularly the 'dramatic helmet removal' bit). I re-imagined this with a strong willpower tie obviously, and worked that into the special activation setup and the hardness bonus. </div></div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3558-dunecat","user":"dunecat","date":". 08-26-2016, 12:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3558-dunecat","name":"dunecat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}